  This is getting messy. Let's introduce Lagrange's notation:
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notation_for_differentiation#Lagrange's_notation_for_antidifferentiation

  Basically:  g' (x)  =  dg / dx    and    f' ( g (x) )  =  df / dg    and    h' (x)  =  dh / dx


                 dg     f ( g (x) + dg )  -  f ( g (x) )
                ---- * ---------------------------------- * dx
                 dx                    dg
    h' (x)  =  ------------------------------------------------  =  g' (x) * f' ( g (x) )
                                      dx

